{
  "name": "snail",
  "_about": "The garden snail (Cornu aspersum), 6 cm long creeping, its shell 3.5 cm across: a coiled shell of four and a half whorls, glossy, brown with darker spiral bands broken into flecks, a pale lip, carried on its back; the grey-brown wrinkled body gliding out in front of it on its sole, two long eye tentacles and two short feelers. Coats: the grove snail (Cepaea nemoralis): yellow with five dark bands, pink, and plain yellow unbanded. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/soft.py on insectlib.py (one smooth body on a chain of bones that ripples as it crawls).",
